<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">30 October in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 30 October, from 637 to 1961.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/antioch" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/antioch.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/637">637 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,389 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Antioch surrenders to the Arab armies</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After the Battle of the Iron Bridge, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a> surrendered to Muslim forces under Abu Ubayda. The fall of the great Syrian city was part of the rapid conquests that stripped <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> of its eastern provinces.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/antioch">Antioch</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">758 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,268 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Arab and Persian pirates sack Guangzhou</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/an-lushan-rebellion">An Lushan Rebellion</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, Arab and Persian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piracy">pirates</a> sacked the port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangzhou">Guangzhou</a>. In 760, in revenge, Chinese rebels killed thousands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabs">Arabs</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persians">Persians</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yangzhou">Yangzhou</a> massacre.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangzhou">Guangzhou</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1137">1137 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">889 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ranulf of Alife defeats Roger II of Sicily at Rignano</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near Rignano Garganico in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apulia">Apulia</a>, the rebel Ranulf of Alife, supported by troops left behind by Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothair-i">Lothair</a> III, defeated King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roger-ii-of-sicily">Roger II of Sicily</a>. Roger's ally Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sergius-vii-of-naples">Sergius VII of Naples</a> was killed, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> passed under Roger's direct rule.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-rignano">Battle of Rignano</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roger-ii-of-sicily">Roger II of Sicily</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1270">1270 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">756 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Treaty of Tunis ends the Eighth Crusade</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After Louis IX died of disease outside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a>, his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-i-of-anjou">Charles of Anjou</a> negotiated a treaty with the sultan of Tunis and the crusaders withdrew. Louis was canonised in 1297.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">Crusade</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tunis">Tunis</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1340">1340 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">686 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Castile and Portugal defeat the Marinids at Río Salado</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarifa">Tarifa</a>, the kings <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfonso-xi-of-castile">Alfonso XI of Castile</a> and Afonso IV of Portugal defeated the Marinid sultan Abu al-Hasan and Yusuf I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>, who were besieging the town. It was the last major North African attempt to invade <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-rio-salado">Battle of Río Salado</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1485">1485 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">541 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry VII is crowned, beginning the Tudor dynasty</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-vii-of-england">Henry Tudor</a> was crowned at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/westminster-abbey">Westminster Abbey</a> two months after defeating <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-iii-of-england">Richard III</a> at Bosworth. His marriage to Elizabeth of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/york">York</a> united the rival houses of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wars-of-the-roses">Wars of the Roses</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1918">1918 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">108 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Armistice of Mudros takes the Ottomans out of the war</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Ottoman and British representatives signed an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-11-november-1918">armistice</a> aboard HMS <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agamemnon">Agamemnon</a> off <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lemnos">Lemnos</a>. Allied occupation and partition plans followed, provoking the Turkish national movement led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mustafa-kemal-ataturk">Mustafa Kemal</a>.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1938">1938 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">88 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Orson Welles broadcasts The War of the Worlds</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">CBS aired Orson Welles's radio adaptation of H. G. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/well">Wells</a>'s novel as a series of mock news bulletins about a Martian landing in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-jersey">New Jersey</a>. Some listeners were alarmed, though newspapers exaggerated the 'panic'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1961">1961 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">65 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Soviet Union tests the Tsar Bomba</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A Soviet bomber dropped the largest nuclear weapon ever exploded over Novaya Zemlya in the Arctic. Its yield of about 50 megatons was some 3,000 times that of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiroshima">Hiroshima</a> bomb.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hiroshima">Hiroshima</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 30 October <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/andrew-duke-of-calabria"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Andrew, Duke of Calabria</span><span class="tp">1327–1345</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/lucas-watzenrode"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/lucas-watzenrode.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Lucas Watzenrode</span><span class="tp">1447–1512</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/francisco-i-madero"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francisco-i-madero.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Francisco I. Madero</span><span class="tp">1873–1913</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/leabua-jonathan"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/leabua-jonathan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Leabua Jonathan</span><span class="tp">1914–1987</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 30 October <span class="n">6</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sergius-vii-of-naples"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Sergius VII of Naples</span><span class="tp">d. 1137</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ibn-khallikan"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Ibn Khallikan</span><span class="tp">1211–1282</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/edward-vernon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/edward-vernon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Edward Vernon</span><span class="tp">1684–1757</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/frederick-i-of-wurttemberg"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/frederick-i-of-wurttemberg.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Frederick I of Württemberg</span><span class="tp">1754–1816</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/henry-dunant"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/henry-dunant.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Henry Dunant</span><span class="tp">1828–1910</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/bonar-law"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/bonar-law.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Bonar Law</span><span class="tp">1858–1923</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
